lobal:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both required filesystems are directly observed with nosuid,nodev,noexec after a real node reboot, with writable 1777 directories, successful fstab validation, and no failed units. The mandatory restart protocol is coherent: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and connection interruption, changed boot identity, and recovered mount/system health.","limitations":["The nosuid property was verified directly as a mount option, but its behavioral effect was not isolated from noexec because the same test file could not execute.","No separate application, persistent-data, or cluster workload existed in the supplied evidence; restart recovery checks therefore covered node health and the task-relevant mounts."]}
